#EXTINF:2612 group-title="Non Fiction Religion Other Religions",The Golden Bough A Study In Magic And Religion Part Iv Adonis Attis Osiris Volume I — James Frazer · III. ADONIS IN CYPRUS. Phoenician colonies in Cyrpus- Kingdom of paphos- Sanctuary of Aphrodite at Paphos- The Aphrodite of Paphos a Phoenician or aboriginal deity- Her conical image- Sacred prostitution in th worship of the Paphian Aphrodoite and of other Asiatic goddesses- The Asiatic Mother Goddess a personification of all the reproductive energies of nature- Her worship reflects a period of sexual communism- The daughters of Cinyras with his daughter Myrrha and birth of Adonis- Suggested explanation of legends of royal incest- The Flamen Dialis and his Flaminica at Rome- Indian parallesl- Cinyras beloved by Aphrodite- Pygmalian and Aphrodite- The Phoenician kings of Cyprus and thier sons the hereditary lovers of the goddess- The father and mother of a god- Cinyras as a musician- The uses of music in religion- Traditions as to the death of Cinyras. - Read by Leon Harvey - Duration 00:43:32
